1. Azure Cloud Architecture

Azure Cloud Architecture is the way Microsoft Azure services are organized to deliver applications, storage, networking, security, and computing resources.

Basic Azure Architecture Layers:

1) Azure Tenant:
       i) Identity and access management.
      ii) Users, groups, and applications are managed here.

2) Azure Subscription:
       i) Billing and resource management boundary.
      ii) Resources are created under a subscription.

3) Resource Group:
       i) Logical container for resources.

4) Resources: 
       i) Virtual Machines (VMs)
      ii) Storage Accounts
     iii) Databases
      iv) Virtual Networks
       v) App Services, etc.
Example:

Tenant-->Subscription--->Resource Group ---> 1) Virtual Machine
                                             2) Storage Account
                                             3) SQL Database



