4. Importance of Azure Resource Group


A Resource Group is a logical container that holds related Azure resources.

Why Resource Groups Are Important:

      1] Organize Resources
               *Keep all project resources together.

      2] Easy Management
               *Manage VM, Storage, Database in one place.
  
      3] Access Control
               *Apply Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) at Resource Group level.

      4] Cost Tracking
               *Monitor costs project-wise.
  
      5] Deployment Management
               *Deploy and delete resources as a single unit.

      6] Lifecycle Management
               *When a project ends, deleting the Resource Group removes all resources inside it.

